# branch feature/cc1-cc2 tip 63a379bc028775b80c402649c89df5025437b2e3
From 8721c8cac296198279e19bb8749f47dd11f0f15c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: spotUP <retroranksmail@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 21:34:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] chips: the custom chips' decisions apart from the OS
 calls (CC1, CC2)

render/chips.c holds what the blitter scroll and the sprite cursor decide,
host-tested in the make test glob (suite chips):
- CC1: the scroll's plan (the rows a BltBitMap copy moves, the rows it
  vacates and owes to the CPU painter, the rows it keeps busy), whether
  the CPU may write rows beside a pending copy without a WaitBlit, and
  when a scroll goes by blit at all.
- CC2: the cursor's rectangle per DECSCUSR shape, a cell as sprite pixels
  and lines (screen and sprite pixel widths in ns, laced), the MoveSprite
  position in lores units, the 2-plane sprite image (block in colour 1,
  the glyph in colour 2; refused where a coarser sprite cannot show the
  glyph), the sprite's colour registers (refused where they are text
  colours), and the order of the fallbacks to the plane cursor.

painter: vp_fill / vp_fill_fast -- n cells in one pen at any bit phase,
through the 68k plane loop's constant path; tested against the pixel
model and equal to vp_span in one pen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
