From a56ae8176ebaf7ca9841001b2408dcbb7d991be4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: spotUP <retroranksmail@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 21:34:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] render: CC1 scroll by blitter copy beside the CPU
 painter, CC2 sprite cursor

CC1. Inside a render pass on an unobscured planar window (planes_ok: chip
RAM, one clip rectangle, an 8-pixel font) raw_scroll is one BltBitMap copy
of the planes in use -- no ScrollRaster, no clearing blit. The rows it
vacates are owed (owe0..owe1) and filled by the painter (vp_fill_fast):
before draw_rows draws on them (whose default blanks then need no fill),
before the cursor, before another scroll would move them, at the end of
the pass. CPU writes go through cpu_sync: no WaitBlit when the only blit
that may run is the scroll copy and the rows are outside it (a region
scroll's status rows); every other graphics call marks the blitter busy
anywhere (GFX). vr_mask_end does the pass's one WaitBlit, so WaitForChar
still answers after every pixel is drawn. Covered windows, RTG and other
fonts keep ScrollRaster. The DIRECT=1 blit-and-blit-fill scroll is gone:
this path replaces it.

CC2. vr_cursor_on puts the cursor in a hardware sprite when it can
(spr_show): an ExtSprite from AllocSpriteDataA, GetExtSpriteA on sprites
2,4,6,3,5,7 whose colour registers are not text colours (16-colour
screens: Workbench or UP-Term's own), the cell in the cursor colour and a
block's glyph in the background colour, MoveSprite when only the position
changes. No cursor erase and draw in the planes per flush: vr_cursor_off
leaves a sprite where it is; vr_cursor_hide (blink, a tab going, the
scrollback) takes it away. Falls back to the plane cursor when the
display is RTG / scan doubled, the window is covered or inactive or its
screen not in front, the cell is not whole sprite pixels and lines or its
corner between two positions, the cell is a double-size row or a glyph
not from the bitmap font (or one a coarser sprite cannot show), no sprite
is free. The frame clock watches a shown sprite (vr_cursor_watch: cover,
screen order, the pointer's sprite resolution); focus changes decide
again. vr_free and a tab going off give the sprite back (a never-freed
blank image shown, colour registers restored).

Reachability: the renderer counts both paths (n_blit_scroll, n_owed_fill,
n_spr_moves, n_spr_images, n_plane_cursor, spr_env); the handler writes
them at ACTION_END; tools/rig/cc_rig.py runs a SERIAL=1 handler through
vtwin's flush on the rig, own screen and Workbench, and requires them.

